WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.483
For the fictional review, use a user
requirements specification, or URS, at

2
00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:09.869
revision three, drawing revision B and
risk record revision two.

3
00:00:09.989 --> 00:00:12.720
These references are teaching
placeholders.

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.149
A baseline is the defined set of
information used for the review.

5
00:00:17.269 --> 00:00:22.133
If one reviewer reads revision A while
another reads revision B, apparent

6
00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:24.621
agreement may hide a different design.

7
00:00:24.741 --> 00:00:29.435
Record the document identifiers, revisions
and approval status together.

8
00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:33.959
Suppose the process team has not defined
the batch-volume range.

9
00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:39.071
The supplier offers a vessel capacity, but
a catalogue capacity is not an

10
00:00:39.191 --> 00:00:40.791
agreed process need.

11
00:00:40.911 --> 00:00:44.903
Raise a question to the process owner and
record the consequence for

12
00:00:45.023 --> 00:00:48.073
impeller location and mixing verification.

13
00:00:48.193 --> 00:00:53.036
The design review may examine unrelated
matters, but it cannot conclude that

14
00:00:53.156 --> 00:00:56.484
mixing is suitable across an unspecified
range.

15
00:00:56.604 --> 00:00:58.716
Unknown inputs should stay visible.

16
00:00:59.336 --> 00:01:02.148
An arrangement drawing shows physical
placement.

17
00:01:02.268 --> 00:01:05.745
A piping and instrumentation diagram shows
process

18
00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.614
connections and instruments.

19
00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:12.150
A functional specification describes
intended control behaviour.

20
00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.836
Our teaching package also includes
material specifications, a cleaning

21
00:01:16.956 --> 00:01:19.324
concept and an interface register.

22
00:01:19.444 --> 00:01:21.982
These documents answer different
questions.

23
00:01:22.102 --> 00:01:26.860
A drawing label such as temperature
control does not describe alarm delays,

24
00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:30.201
sensor failure responses or operator
permissions.

25
00:01:30.321 --> 00:01:33.489
Request the document that actually
supports the claim.

26
00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:38.909
During review, the supplier issues
revision C with a different outlet valve.

27
00:01:39.029 --> 00:01:42.912
Do not silently replace the drawing and
keep the old signatures.

28
00:01:43.032 --> 00:01:47.747
Compare the change, identify affected
requirements and risks, and obtain

29
00:01:47.867 --> 00:01:49.360
the appropriate review.

30
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:53.811
Record which conclusions remain applicable
and which need reassessment.

31
00:01:53.931 --> 00:01:58.389
The goal is not to restart every check
automatically, but to prevent an

32
00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:01.987
unreviewed design from inheriting an
earlier conclusion.
